 "said": {
  "text": "'It only detects words when I press speak' in AmberX (apps/amberx-droid). Cause: the native wake listener runs only while 'Watch axHub in the background' is on (default off) and pauses while the app is on screen. Fix: hands-free listening is its own setting (default on), works on screen and in the background, independent of axHub monitoring; optional always-armed (no wake phrase). Plus a detection overlay like ActiveX: floating draggable window over other apps with a moving audio-level line graph, decibel number, what was heard, and quick settings (listening on/off, always armed, hide). Colours from the app's theme tokens. Profile refactor, Opus (Brett's pick). Android exception: AmberX shell is allowed (rule Oct 25).",
  "verbatim": false,
  "at": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
